        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" type="taisho" xlink:href="T_223">
            <c:note/>
            <c:pages>250b3-7</c:pages>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="AnTingshan1997">
            <c:pages>128</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">An Tingshan mentions the inscription without identifying it and gives
                the measurements of the character <hi rend="italic">san</hi>
                <foreign xml:lang="zh">散</foreign>.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">安廷山提及此處銘文，但沒有確定該銘文出處，並提供了“散”字的測量數據。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="XuQing2000">
            <c:pages>4</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Xu Qing briefly mentions the inscription, but does not identify the
                text passage.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">徐清簡短提及此處銘文，但沒有給出節文出處。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="ZhangZong2000a">
            <c:pages>66-68</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Zhang Zong identifies the text passage as taken from the <hi rend="italic">Great Perfection of Wisdom Sutra</hi> (<hi rend="italic">
                    <foreign xml:lang="sa">Mahāprajñāpāramitā-sūtra</foreign>
                </hi>), compares it to
                Dunhuang manuscripts and relates it to Nanyue Huisi.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">張總認定節文出自《般若波羅蜜經》，並將其與敦煌寫經相比較，指出其與南嶽慧思的關係。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LaiFei2000a">
            <c:pages>265</c:pages>
            <c:note>Lai Fei dates the inscription around the year 564.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">賴非將此處刻經的年代定為公元564年前後。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="XuHongguo2000">
            <c:pages>34</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Xu Hongguo dates the inscription around the year 564.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">許洪國將此處刻經的年代定為公元564年前後。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="ZhangZong2003a">
            <c:pages>9-10, 24</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Zhang Zong identifies the text passage also in the <hi rend="italic">Treatise on the Great Perfection of Wisdom</hi>, <hi rend="italic">Da zhidu
                    lun</hi>, compares it to the inscription on the single boulder on Mount Culai,
                which is located east of Guanghua Monastery, and also discusses the Eighteen Aspects
                of Emptiness.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">張總認定節文也出現在《大智度論》中，將其與位於徂徠山光化寺東面一處巨石的題刻進行比較，並且論及“十八空”。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LaiFei2003c">
            <c:pages>125-126</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Lai Fei identifies the inscription as a text on the Eighteen Aspects
                of Emptiness and relates it to the inscription on the boulder on Mount
                Culai.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">賴非確定該銘文是有關“十八空”的經文，並與徂徠山巨石上的題刻相聯繫。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="Kiriya2003a">
            <c:pages>74</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Kiriya remarks that the rock cut sutras stand in the tradition of
                Chinese stone stelae, starting in the Eastern Han dynasty, as this inscription and
                the giant stone stele at Mount Tie show.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">桐谷征一評述說，石刻佛經屬於東漢以來中國碑刻的傳統，正如該銘文和鐵山巨大的石碑所示。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="Harrist2004">
            <c:pages>10-11</c:pages>
            <c:note lang="en">Harrist sees the inscription as a predecessor of the sutra text carved
                at Mount Tie and characterizes it as a “virtual stele.”</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">韓文彬認為此銘文是鐵山刻經的先例，並形容它為“虛擬之碑”。</c:note>
        </c:ref>
        <c:ref xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" value="discussion" type="modern" xlink:href="LaiFei2007">
            <c:note lang="en">Lai Fei gives the inscription’s location, its measurements and a
                description of the carved stele decor, as well as a reconstruction of the unfinished
                text. He also describes the remaining three characters’ state of preservation, see
                also <ref type="biblio" target="LaiFei2004">107</ref>.</c:note>
            <c:note lang="zh">賴非提供了題刻的位置和測量數據，描述了刻在石碑上的裝飾，並復原了該未完成的文本。他還描述了殘餘的三個字的保存狀況，參見<ref type="biblio" target="LaiFei2004">107</ref>。</c:note>
            <c:pages>21-23</c:pages>
        </c:ref>
    </c:references>
